=== SURVEY ===
SURVEY_PHASE_NOTE: Read internal/platform/httputil/logging.go, client.go, logging_test.go, client_test.go,
internal/api/api_call_log_middleware.go, cmd/teslasync/main.go, internal/models/tesla.go (APICallLog).

httputil.LoggedTransport currently only emits zerolog lines; no sink. ClientConfig has no Sink field.
sanitizeURL redacts only key/token/secret (not password). The new RedactURL must extend the rule
set to match the inbound regex (?i)token|key|secret|password.

internal/api.APICallLogger interface (Prompt 10) is the production async writer. It takes
*models.APICallLog. The new httputil.APICallSink takes httputil.APICallRecord (defined locally
in httputil so the package never imports internal/database or internal/models). The adapter
in internal/api converts APICallRecord -> *models.APICallLog and calls APICallLogger.Enqueue.

Tesla outbound paths:
  - internal/tesla/client.go uses *http.Client directly (no httputil.NewClient, verified by grep).
  - SetLogCallback in main.go remains the canonical persistence path for service="tesla-api".
  - No double-record because the Tesla client never opts into the new Sink.

httputil.NewClient call sites in production: NONE (only client_test.go). Therefore wiring the
adapter into "every httputil.NewClient call introduced in Prompt 13" is a no-op in main.go for
now; the adapter is constructed and held for future wiring with an explanatory comment.

=== REASONING ===
Implementation plan:
1. New file internal/platform/httputil/sink.go:
   - APICallSink interface { Enqueue(record APICallRecord); CaptureBodies() bool }
   - APICallRecord struct { Service, Method, URL string; StatusCode int; DurationMs int;
                            ErrorMessage string; RequestBody, ResponseBody []byte }
   - Constants: MaxOutboundBodyBytes = 10*1024, OutboundTruncationMarker = "... [truncated]"
   - Helpers: RedactURL(*url.URL) string (uses extended sanitizeURL),
              TruncateBody([]byte, int) []byte
2. Extend internal/platform/httputil/logging.go:
   - sanitizeURL also redacts query params containing "password"
   - LoggedTransport gains Sink APICallSink field
   - In RoundTrip:
     a. If sink != nil and sink.CaptureBodies(), capture request body by reading up to
        MaxOutboundBodyBytes+1 via io.LimitReader, reconstitute req.Body so transport sends
        original bytes (MultiReader for the truncated case).
     b. Defer a sink-only function with an inner recover() so a panicking sink cannot break
        HTTP traffic. The deferred function fires Sink.Enqueue(record) regardless of error.
     c. After successful round-trip, if CaptureBodies, read up to MaxOutboundBodyBytes+1 from
        resp.Body via io.LimitReader; reconstitute resp.Body so the caller still receives the
        full body (NopCloser+MultiReader pattern). Set record.ResponseBody = TruncateBody(...).
     d. Existing zerolog Debug/Error lines are preserved verbatim.
3. Extend internal/platform/httputil/client.go:
   - ClientConfig gains Sink APICallSink (nil-safe).
   - NewClient passes cfg.Sink to LoggedTransport when EnableLogging is true.
4. Extend internal/platform/httputil/logging_test.go with:
   - TestLoggedTransport_SinkRecordsSuccessfulGet (T01)
   - TestLoggedTransport_ServiceTagFromName (T02)
   - TestLoggedTransport_RedactsSensitiveQueryParameters (T04)
   - TestLoggedTransport_BodyCaptureOptInDefaultOff (T06)
   - TestLoggedTransport_BodyCaptureTruncatesAt10KB (T07)
   - TestLoggedTransport_NetworkErrorIsRecorded (T08)
   - TestLoggedTransport_NilSinkIsSafe (T09)
   - TestLoggedTransport_SlowSinkIsNonBlocking (T10) — sink wrapped in goroutine
   - TestLoggedTransport_PreservesExistingZerologLines (T12 — re-runs of existing tests)
   - TestLoggedTransport_EndpointIncludesPathAndRedactedQuery (T13)
   - TestLoggedTransport_ConcurrentRoundTrips (T15)
   - TestLoggedTransport_PanickingSinkRecovered (recover() guard contract)
5. New file internal/platform/httputil/sink_test.go:
   - TestRedactURL_RedactsKeyTokenSecretPassword (T04 sub)
   - TestRedactURL_PreservesNonSensitiveParams
   - TestRedactURL_NilURL
   - TestTruncateBody_PassthroughWhenSmall
   - TestTruncateBody_TruncatesWithMarker
   - TestTruncateBody_ZeroMaxReturnsInput
   - TestLayering_HttputilDoesNotImportDatabase (T11)
6. Extend internal/api/api_call_log_middleware.go:
   - APICallSinkAdapter(logger APICallLogger, captureBodies bool) httputil.APICallSink
   - Internal type apiCallSinkAdapter implements httputil.APICallSink, converts
     APICallRecord -> *models.APICallLog and calls logger.Enqueue.
7. Wire in cmd/teslasync/main.go:
   - Construct outboundAPILogSink := api.APICallSinkAdapter(inboundAPILogger, cfg.APILogs.CaptureBodies)
   - Document with comment that Tesla client uses SetLogCallback (not httputil.NewClient) so
     no double-record occurs. Future non-Tesla adapters wired in Prompt 13 will receive this sink.
   - The variable is referenced via a log.Info() line so Go does not error on unused.

